    "#risk_level()\n",
    "#Days of stock remaining\n",
    "             VS\n",
    "#Supplier delivery time\n",
    "\n",
    "#For example:\n",
    "#Stock remaining = 4 days\n",
    "Supplier lead time = 7 days\n",
    "\n",
    "#Therefore:\n",
    "\n",
    "HIGH / MEDIUM RISK\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the interesting part of the project.
    "\n",
    "#reorder_recommendation()\n",
    "\n",
    "The program doesn't simply say:\n",
    "\n",
    "\"Low stock.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "It calculates approximately how many units should be reordered.\n",
    "\n",
    "That's more useful from a business perspective.\n",
    "\n",
